![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

According to the general rules, we should avoid using `Intl.Collator` with an `undefined` locale for sorting as it can introduce locale-sensitive discrepancies across different runtime environments. Instead, use strict lexicographical byte-order comparison (such as `compareStringsByUtf8ByteOrder`) to ensure locale-independent, deterministic ordering.

```suggestion
  const receipts = [...wave1.receipts, ...bulk.receipts].sort((left, right) => (
    compareStringsByUtf8ByteOrder(left.source_visual_receipt_id, right.source_visual_receipt_id)
    || compareStringsByUtf8ByteOrder(left.question_key, right.question_key)
  ));
  const noReceiptBlockers = [...wave1.noReceiptBlockers, ...bulk.noReceiptBlockers].sort((left, right) => (
    compareStringsByUtf8ByteOrder(left.question_key, right.question_key)
    || compareStringsByUtf8ByteOrder(left.receipt_blocker_status, right.receipt_blocker_status)
  ));
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. Avoid using Intl.Collator with an undefined locale for sorting, as it can introduce locale-sensitive discrepancies across different runtime environments. Instead, use a strict lexicographical byte-order comparison to ensure locale-independent, deterministic ordering.
</details>

